": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887420", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "140097136", "author": {"steamid": "76561198215803696", "personaname": "Mantis", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/ShomotionStudios/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 64, "playtime_forever": 10835, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 10835, "last_played": 1636294372, "avatar": "c01812100a5181939a32a249e6e48827df92b3e8"}, "language": "english", "review": "It wasn't as bad as I heard it was going to be but it was a little weird too.  I would have just continued to build on the characters in the original galaxy.  Going to Andromeda seemed a little odd.  Don't outsource your facial animation team is another lesson learned I guess.  They made it seem like this was going to be some kind of miracle of realism or something but the end product is basically the exact opposite.   The character design was just off for some reason.  The Aliens were cool, but the humans just looked really dead inside.  \n\nGameplay is ok, but nothing groundbreaking.\nPlot kinda felt like it dragged on a bit too much.\nIts playable if you want more mass effecty type stuff but its not a fun as the original games.  \nThey really should have just made a mass effect prequel or explored the consequences of the ending of the original game.\n\n5/10 - meh game.", "timestamp_created": 1686833296, "timestamp_updated": 1686833296, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887420", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "140077502", "author": {"steamid": "76561198061985439", "personaname": "jinx101", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/jinx101